# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
#  TEMPLATE ONLY — placeholders. Never put a real key in THIS file.
#  This file lives in the repo and is committed. That is safe precisely because
#  it contains nothing.
#
#  THE REAL FILE GOES OUTSIDE THE REPO:
#
#      C:\Users\hp\.banknifty-copilot\.env
#
#  Copy it there in one command (PowerShell, from the repo root):
#
#      New-Item -ItemType Directory -Force "$HOME\.banknifty-copilot" | Out-Null
#      Copy-Item .env.example "$HOME\.banknifty-copilot\.env"
#      notepad "$HOME\.banknifty-copilot\.env"
#
#  Then verify without ever printing the values:
#
#      python tools/fetch_kite.py check
#
#  WHY NOT JUST KEEP IT HERE, GITIGNORED?
#  Because CLAUDE.md §4, KICKOFF §1, BUILD-BRIEF §6 and spec 08 §3.1 all say the
#  same thing: no secret in the repo. A .gitignore is one edit, one `git add -f`,
#  one zip of the folder away from failing. A path outside the repo cannot fail
#  that way. Same convenience, none of the risk — and it matches DECISIONS.md
#  D-015, where the access token cache already lives.
#
#  The loader looks in this order and stops at the first hit:
#      1. process environment
#      2. Windows user environment (registry, HKCU\Environment)
#      3. the .env file above
#  Any of the three works. Use whichever you prefer.
# ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────

# From https://developers.kite.trade → your app. Needed for every call.
KITE_API_KEY=your_api_key_here

# The one that can mint new sessions. Needed only by `fetch_kite.py login`.
KITE_API_SECRET=your_api_secret_here

# Optional. Normally left blank — `login` caches the daily token for you at
# ~/.banknifty-copilot/kite_token.json. Set this only to inject a token by hand.
KITE_ACCESS_TOKEN=
